      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BELLA DANZA (7) is a proven performer at this level. She was narrowly beaten when second at Albion Park last time out, and now that she is racing from the Grimson yard, she is the one to beat. LUX AETERNA (10) is another quality mare who was narrowly beaten into third here 2 weeks ago in a strong field. That form reads extremely well for this and if she has some luck from a much tougher gate, she looms as the main danger to the top pick. STENO (9) faces a sharp rise in grade after finishing third at Albion Park, but her effort was sound and with a strong record on this circuit, she can figure in the top 3 again. GOLLY GEE FELLAS (4) resumes from a spell, and she has been trialling up nicely. She has a good gate, and will be ready to rumble fresh up. Follow the market moves. THE ANSWER (6) finished well back in a Group One here last start in May. She comes to hand quickly, and is worthy of respect.",
